https://t.co/X7ipfsWjp2’s Free Speech Tracker had documented the censorship of How Modi and Adani Stole India | The Friendship Files, a 36-minute documentary by Sabeer Bhatia (@sabeer) that was blocked on YouTube in India. We condemn the Mumbai Police notice directing X to remove posts about the documentary, citing alleged false and disparaging statements, and invoking provisions of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita.

The use of criminal law to address online criticism, particularly without direct notice to affected users, risks penalising legitimate expression and creating a chilling effect on free speech. Criminal provisions must not become a means of curtailing online criticism and debate on matters of public interest.

